// setStream Associates a CUDA stream with a cuFFT plan.
//
// Note that starting from CUDA 11.2 (cuFFT 10.4.0), [Handle.SetStream] is supported on multi-GPU plans. When associating a stream with a plan, cufftXtMemcpy() remains synchronous across the multiple GPUs. For previous versions of cuFFT, [Handle.SetStream] will return an error in multiple GPU plans. Note that starting from CUDA 12.2 (cuFFT 11.0.8), on multi-GPU plans, stream can be associated with any context on any GPU. However, repeated calls to [Handle.SetStream] with streams from different contexts incur a small time penalty. Optimal performance is obtained when repeated calls to [Handle.SetStream] use streams from the same CUDA context.
//
//   - plan: The [Handle] object to associate with the stream
//   - stream: A valid CUDA stream created with cudaStreamCreate(); 0 for the default stream
//
// Returns:
//   - InvalidPlan: The plan parameter is not a valid handle, or plan is multi-gpu in cuFFT version prior to 10.4.0.
//   - Success: The stream was associated with the plan.
//
// Wraps cufftSetStream.
func setStream(plan Handle, stream Stream) error {
	if err := checkLibSym("cufftSetStream"); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return toError(fnsetStream(plan, stream))
}

// setWorkArea [Handle.SetWorkArea] overrides the work area pointer associated with a plan.
//
// If the work area was auto-allocated, cuFFT frees the auto-allocated space. The cufftExec*() calls assume that the work area pointer is valid and that it points to a contiguous region in device memory that does not overlap with any other work area. If this is not the case, results are indeterminate.
//
//   - plan: [Handle] returned by [Create]
//
// Returns:
//   - InternalError: An internal driver error was detected.
//   - InvalidPlan: The plan parameter is not a valid handle.
//   - SetupFailed: The cuFFT library failed to initialize.
//   - Success: cuFFT successfully returned the size of the work space.
//
// Wraps cufftSetWorkArea.
func setWorkArea(plan Handle, workArea uintptr) error {
	if err := checkLibSym("cufftSetWorkArea"); err != nil {
		return err
	}
	return toError(fnsetWorkArea(plan, workArea))
}
